title: "pallet-identity: return username deposits to the authority that paid them"
doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      Fixes #13680. A username deposit is reserved from the authority that grants the username,
      but `remove_expired_approval`, `remove_username` and `kill_username` refunded or slashed
      whichever account was the authority of the suffix at that time. After the suffix was moved
      to another account with `add_username_authority`, the previous authority's deposits stayed
      reserved forever, and the new authority had unrelated reserved funds released, or was
      slashed instead. After `remove_username_authority`, the deposits could not be released at
      all.

      The pallet now records the depositor of each deposit-backed username in the new storage
      item `UsernameDepositor`, and the three calls refund or slash that account. Usernames
      granted before this change have no record and keep the previous behaviour, so no migration
      is needed.
crates:
  - name: pallet-identity
    bump: minor
